=== P6E-E02: live re-verification of Havenask's two Phase 6B/6C blockers ===

--- docker/dockerd binary presence ---
$ which bazel bazelisk
(no output -- neither found)
$ which docker dockerd
/usr/bin/docker
/usr/bin/dockerd
$ docker version
Client: Docker Engine - Community
 Version: 29.3.1
Server:
failed to connect to the docker API at unix:///var/run/docker.sock; check if
the path is correct and if the daemon is running: dial unix
/var/run/docker.sock: connect: no such file or directory
$ systemctl status docker
System has not been booted with systemd as init system (PID 1). Can't operate.
Failed to connect to bus: Host is down

--- manually starting dockerd (no systemd) ---
$ nohup dockerd > /tmp/dockerd.log 2>&1 &
[dockerd log shows containerd booting, "Daemon has completed initialization",
"API listen on /var/run/docker.sock"]
$ docker info
Server:
 Containers: 0
 Images: 0
 Server Version: 29.3.1
 Storage Driver: overlayfs
[daemon fully functional -- a real change from Phase 6B/6C's "Docker
daemon absent" finding]

--- attempting real image pulls across multiple registries ---
$ docker run --rm hello-world
Pulling from library/hello-world
failed to copy: httpReadSeeker: failed open: failed to do request:
Get "https://production.cloudfront.docker.com/registry-v2/.../data?...": Forbidden

$ docker pull ghcr.io/homebrew/core/hello:2.12.1
Pulling from homebrew/core/hello
failed to copy: httpReadSeeker: failed open: failed to do request:
Get "https://pkg-containers.githubusercontent.com/ghcr1/blobs/sha256:...": Forbidden

$ docker pull public.ecr.aws/docker/library/hello-world:latest
Pulling from docker/library/hello-world
failed to copy: httpReadSeeker: failed open: failed to do request:
Get "https://d2glxqk2uabbnd.cloudfront.net/v2/...": Forbidden

--- registry API reachability (metadata/auth layer only) ---
$ curl -o /dev/null -w "HTTP:%{http_code}\n" https://ghcr.io/v2/
HTTP:401   (normal: auth required, host itself reachable)
$ curl -o /dev/null -w "HTTP:%{http_code}\n" https://registry-1.docker.io/v2/
HTTP:401   (normal: auth required, host itself reachable)

--- Havenask's own registry (unchanged from Phase 6B/6C) ---
$ curl -o /dev/null -w "HTTP:%{http_code}\n" https://registry.cn-hangzhou.aliyuncs.com/v2/
curl: (56) CONNECT tunnel failed, response 403
HTTP:000   (blocked at the connection/proxy level, not just auth)
$ curl -o /dev/null -w "HTTP:%{http_code}\n" https://quay.io/v2/
curl: (56) CONNECT tunnel failed, response 403
HTTP:000   (also blocked at the connection level -- not every registry
            gets even the metadata-API-level access ghcr.io/Docker Hub do)

--- searching for a Havenask mirror on Docker Hub ---
$ for repo in havenask/havenask alibaba/havenask havenask/ha3 havenask/suez; do
    curl https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/$repo/
  done
{"message":"object not found","errinfo":{}}   (x4, no mirror found under
                                                any plausible name)

--- cleanup ---
$ pkill -f dockerd
$ ps aux | grep -iE "docker|containerd" | grep -v grep
(no output -- confirmed fully stopped, no lingering processes)

=== Conclusion ===
Docker daemon itself: now functional (real change from "absent").
Container image pulls: blocked network-wide across every registry
tested (Docker Hub, ghcr.io, AWS public ECR mirror) -- blob/CDN storage
hosts specifically, not registry API hosts.
Havenask's own registry: still blocked at the connection level,
unchanged from Phase 6B/6C.
Net effect on Havenask's availability: UNCHANGED -- still genuinely
blocked, now for a more precisely characterized reason.
